3042 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate ${\\int }_{C}(3x+y)\\,dx+x\\,dy,$ where $C$ is a portion of the parabola parametrized by $r(t)={t}^{2}\\,i+(4t-1)\\,j$ for $t\\in [0,2].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413042 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7e1c746b-98be-5a3b-93f3-3c945fad75be" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413042 #edb/ref 1074 "Along the curve, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)={t}^{2},\\,y(t)=4t-1.\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4t-1)\\,j \\\\  & =2t\\,i+4\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can calculate the line integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}(3x+y)\\,dx+x\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(3x+y)\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt+x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}((3x+y)\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(3{t}^{2}+4t-1)\\cdot 2t+{t}^{2}\\cdot 4\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}6{t}^{3}+8{t}^{2}-2t+4{t}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}6{t}^{3}+12{t}^{2}-2t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={[\\frac{3}{2}{t}^{4}+4{t}^{3}-{t}^{2}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =[\\frac{3}{2}(2)^{4}+4(2)^{3}-{2}^{2}]-[0] \\\\  & =[24+32-4] \\\\  & =52\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429164 #edb/ref 1030 1.0 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186429164 #edb/ref 1032 "Initial Codex estimate from captured target-band crossing frequency. Selected account multivariable: 1 rises / 1 eligible passed source activities = 1.000000; nearest selected fraction = 1. Crossing activity numbers [1]; waits [1]. Separate account estimates: multivariable=1 (1/1). Selection: most observations, then lower weight, then account name; no averaging. Single-activity estimates included. Intervening target updates: False. Crossing frequency is the chosen practical estimate of encompassing coverage; a mult